The private POST and GET implementations and header/JSON helpers preserve the
existing under-limit protocol behavior and diagnostic redaction. Non-streaming
bodies use the 3.9.0 streamed byte limits. SSE event accounting retains upstream's
limiter; a boxed stream/unfold replaces its pin-projected wrapper and checks the
terminal state before polling another chunk. GET preserves the existing reqwest
status-error category; DELETE remains delegated to rmcp. Credential-bearing
request URLs, raw reflected non-protocol bodies, authentication hints and content
type values are omitted from diagnostics. Oversized bodies remain typed errors.
